    materials: [
      { text: 'added servo slots and CF tube pockets for reinforcement....', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 05, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Add 4mm carbon tube spars to wing and vert fuse in.', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Aug 28, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I gouged and poked at them and was able to remove about half, then I placed a small amount of CA glue on the end of the brass tube, inserted the tube while rotating it about half a turn, counted to 15 then rotated the brass tube and…', author: 'JonathanPM', date: 'Dec 27, 2016', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Unless you want to pay a $20 premium for nice white Aero Depron....', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 23, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Fuselage joined together with 6mm carbon tubing from ModelPlaneFoam.com.', author: 'JonathanPM', date: 'Dec 20, 2016', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Using 2 Robart "Large" pinned hinges with 30 minute epoxy.', author: 'JonathanPM', date: 'Dec 22, 2016', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    electronics: [
      { text: 'I like the idea of the ducted fan/prop in a slot look and i wanted it to be as scale as possible.', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 05, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I ended up going with seperate servos for each aileron and each elevator because of routing and stuff.', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 05, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I want to mix in some flaps at the ailerons and maybe mix the ailerons into the elevators..', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 05, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Maybe a higher KV motor would do it but watch your amps!', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 05, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'CG is right on the front of the center of the prop slot or forward a little.', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 05, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I used a 9g servo for each control surface and mixed everything together.', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 05, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'added servo slots and CF tube pockets for reinforcement....', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 05, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Servo notch is the top and goes against the bottom of the wing 7.', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Aug 28, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Cut out a 1 1/4" round firewall from plywood and glue into the motor slot 11.', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Aug 28, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Need to have a servo for each control surface.', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Aug 28, 2011', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    balance: [
      { text: 'First flight was a little wierd while i was getting CG right and all the trims and mixes worked out and i ended up nosing it in and snapping the front end off.', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 05, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'It actually flew better without it so i decided that it had a little bit too much vertical ahead of the CG so i cut off the vertical stab and put on a 25% larger one.', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 05, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'CG is right on the front of the center of the prop slot or forward a little.', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 05, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'The CG note is on the first post basically it is in the center of the Prop Slot.', author: 'SGTalon', date: 'Jul 15, 2011', source: 'thread' },
    ],
