    threads: [
      { url: 'http://www.rcgroups.com/forums/showthread.php?t=899413', label: 'RC GROUPS BUILD THREAD', external: true },
    ],
    materials: [
      { text: 'It is built from 6 mm Depron, held together with hot glue.', author: 'nac', date: 'Jul 25, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I used Epoxy for the carbon rods and motor mount.', author: 'nac', date: 'Jul 25, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Using a full span 6x1 mm carbon strip for the main spar with a 3 mm carbon tube secondary spar immediately in front of the motor mount location.', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Mar 27, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'As I am using 13" x 39" 6 mm depron, I CA\'d two pieces for the horizontal parts (wing / fuselage) which limited me to a 26 1/2" span vice 27 1/2".', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Mar 27, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I am also mulling the idea of laminating two more layers of 6 mm depron to the fuselage vertical profile piece for a semi-3D look as well as added strength in the nose (landing insurance?).', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Mar 27, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'In the pictures of the original build in post 1 or 2 it shows an additional carbon rod bracing the lower portions of the fin and fuselage electronics enclosure ends.', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Mar 27, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I would use 3mm depron for all of the plane except for the center fuse and vertical stab pieces.', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Nov 11, 2010', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'For the wing spar you can use 2mm carbon fiber tube.', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Nov 11, 2010', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Mike Found a planset for this model in my plans collection, then found this posting and cheked my motor collection (SUCCESS!!!) Now to put together a shopping list for the LHS and to check my collection of 6mm depron as well as the local…', author: 'byrocat', date: 'Apr 30, 2023', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Even if you went with 6mm depron, you should be able to be under 120g AUW, including battery.', author: 'Fly_Bye', date: 'Oct 06, 2010', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    electronics: [
      { text: 'It keeps the simple form of thrust vectoring by having the control surfaces in the prop wash from a mid-mounted motor.', author: 'nac', date: 'Jul 25, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I used Epoxy for the carbon rods and motor mount.', author: 'nac', date: 'Jul 25, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'SPECS:- Wing span = 70cm (27.5”) Length = 92cm (36”) MY SETEP:- AUW (with battery & painted) = 532g Prop = 6x4 Motor = 2000kv ESC = 40 Amp Battery = 2170mAh 3s1p Li-Po Aileron throw = +/- 20 degrees Static thrust = 650g NOTE: I have only…', author: 'nac', date: 'Jul 25, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Mike Found a planset for this model in my plans collection, then found this posting and cheked my motor collection (SUCCESS!!!) Now to put together a shopping list for the LHS and to check my collection of 6mm depron as well as the local…', author: 'byrocat', date: 'Apr 30, 2023', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Today I got more velcro in her with the battery moved forward just a hair, and it\'s perfect now!', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Dec 27, 2010', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Motor - 1806N 2500 kv ESC - 10A HK ESC GWS 4530 prop 2x HXT500 servos Hyperion 3S 850mAh lipo Not sure of the AUW, need to weigh her.', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Dec 27, 2010', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Here are my final stats: Motor - AX 1806N 2500kv 18-gram outrunner ESC - Hobby King SS 10A Servos - 2x HXT500 5-gram Prop - GWS 4530 Battery - Hyperion CX G3 850mAh 3S 25C RX - XPS Nano-E 6-ch Dry weight - 3.8oz, 107 grams AUW - 6.2oz, 177…', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Jan 01, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Servos were in the called for location, 2212-06 Suppo, 35A Waypoint ESC, 6x4 APC prop, 6ch OrangeRX (plastic case removed).', author: 'Mazzepa1', date: 'Jul 12, 2014', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I couldn\'t get it to balance with anything less than an 1800 mah and the ESC all the way forward.', author: 'Mazzepa1', date: 'Jul 12, 2014', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'It flew great, but I\'m encouraged now to get this one set up to balance w/a 1320 mah battery just to see what a lighter F4D would fly like.', author: 'Mazzepa1', date: 'Jul 12, 2014', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    balance: [
      { text: 'I couldn\'t get it to balance with anything less than an 1800 mah and the ESC all the way forward.', author: 'Mazzepa1', date: 'Jul 12, 2014', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'It flew great, but I\'m encouraged now to get this one set up to balance w/a 1320 mah battery just to see what a lighter F4D would fly like.', author: 'Mazzepa1', date: 'Jul 12, 2014', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I carefully went over all my controls and weights and found my marked CG was back slightly from the 75% plans\' suggestion......a mistake I made as I was converting inch to MM it seems Wasn\'t much, maybe 1/4in but that made all the…', author: 'Wrench66', date: 'Oct 03, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'By adding a couple of small metal washers into her nose and moving the CG forward a skoosh, the plane now reacts totally differently in flight......in the wind it\'s very floaty and a NICE challenge.', author: 'Wrench66', date: 'Oct 03, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I did move the CG forward and it helped some but the slow speed stuff just worsened so that\'s not the whole answer Out of the three batteries I tried I just couldn\'t get comfortable with the plane unfortunately.', author: 'Wrench66', date: 'Sep 30, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'It will balance with a 1300 or a 2200 so I made some marks inside for both.', author: 'beemerdon', date: 'Dec 06, 2011', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    finishing: [
      { text: 'SPECS:- Wing span = 70cm (27.5”) Length = 92cm (36”) MY SETEP:- AUW (with battery & painted) = 532g Prop = 6x4 Motor = 2000kv ESC = 40 Amp Battery = 2170mAh 3s1p Li-Po Aileron throw = +/- 20 degrees Static thrust = 650g NOTE: I have only…', author: 'nac', date: 'Jul 25, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Still all white, just need to add some paint and decals.', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Dec 27, 2010', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I now have paint on it, but need to run to the store tomorrow as I ran out of one color and have some touch ups to do.', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Dec 19, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'So I finally got some paint and decals on my mini.', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Jan 01, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I am going to paint it up and get some decals on it then post a pic or 2 of the fan install........', author: 'nac', date: 'Jan 19, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I brought it home and finished all the painting, and then started on the decals.', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Dec 21, 2008', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    flightNotes: [
      { text: 'Flew her on Friday morning and what a delight!', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Dec 27, 2010', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'First flight was a little tail heavy, and the velcro pulled out on me, so no more flights that day.', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Dec 27, 2010', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'She will even do the famous hands off flat spin just like her big sister!', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Dec 27, 2010', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'He let me have the privilege of the first flight.', author: 'eliworm', date: 'Feb 13, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'It flys every good as it\'s big brother and does that great hands off Skyray spin.', author: 'eliworm', date: 'Feb 13, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'After we both flew it a number of time our only complaint is the centering of the junk Hobby City servos.', author: 'eliworm', date: 'Feb 13, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Funny that you happen to revive this thread as I flew an old friend today.', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Apr 02, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'But I fixed the minor issues and flew her today just to make sure all was well.', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Apr 02, 2011', source: 'thread' },
    ],
