    materials: [
      { text: 'i want to ask it is save to fly when i only have a 5mm depron for wing..', author: 'CHATCHAIAPI', date: 'Dec 20, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'we spar the wing with 6mm CF tube and made a KF-2 wing so it strong enough even 100% throttle and sport flying.', author: 'CHATCHAIAPI', date: 'Dec 20, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'With the KFm2 wing does it still need a 6mm carbon tube or would a 6x1mm flat be sufficient as the spar?', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Mar 12, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Adhesives will be a mix of Foam-Tac, CA and epoxy used where appropriate.', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Mar 12, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Depron Mermaid on grass (1 min 36 sec) The wing span is 1050mm (41").', author: 'vleisie', date: 'Feb 25, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Construction is all 6mm depron with some carbon and plywood reinforcement.', author: 'vleisie', date: 'Feb 25, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'If it is made of a single layer of foam thickness of 6 mm, a carbon rod is inserted, the same having a diameter of 6 mm?', author: 'vleisie', date: 'Mar 05, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Hi Vladimir, The original plans are for a wing made from a single layer of foam with a 6mm diameter carbon tube wing spar.', author: 'vleisie', date: 'Mar 05, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Put the tube in the slot and glue with epoxy to fill up the gaps between the tube and the foam.', author: 'vleisie', date: 'Mar 05, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I built it with the Kfm 2 wing and installed a 4mm carbon fiber tube for a spar.', author: 'Rolland Benson', date: 'Jul 01, 2013', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    electronics: [
      { text: 'finished mine with the following spec : Quote: D2826-6 2200kv with a 6x4 APC prop.', author: 'TonyTheAsian', date: 'Jan 10, 2014', source: 'thread' },
      { text: '30 amps Plush esc 2x HK 9g white servos ( for aileron, really like these one over the other 9g servo since the thing is so quite ) 2x Turnigy 9g servo.', author: 'TonyTheAsian', date: 'Jan 10, 2014', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'D8R v2 receiver ( super long antenna which allow me to route it toward the back and the wing.', author: 'TonyTheAsian', date: 'Jan 10, 2014', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'The long antenna also allowed me to move the receiver way up front in the lower hull ) 2200 mAH 3s Turnigy battery AUW: w/o battery : 380 grams with 2200 mah battery : 515 grams Not sure if my wing is crooked or my eyes are playing tricks…', author: 'TonyTheAsian', date: 'Jan 10, 2014', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Motors should put up 900g of thrust according to ExperimentalAirline\'s data.', author: 'TonyTheAsian', date: 'Jan 10, 2014', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Next project : A flying wing that use a motor with 1.2kg of thrust for some crazy long endurance.', author: 'TonyTheAsian', date: 'Jan 10, 2014', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I used the following equipment: Motor: 2212-06 (2200kv) Prop: APC 6x4E ESC: 30A+ Lipo: 3S 2200mah Servos: 4x Hitec HS-55 The model is a nice and docile flyer that can do gentle aerobatics.', author: 'vleisie', date: 'Feb 25, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I flew 5 batteries through my Mermaid today flying off the grass of my club field exploring some different configurations.', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Jul 09, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I built this model with a Turigy 2826-6 (2200kv) motor, 40 amp ESC, a 6x4x3 prop, and powered by a 2200mah 3 cell battery.', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Jul 09, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'It has lots of thrust (true vertical climbs) and although it is a bit over-propped it is still within amp limits for the motor which gets quite warm but not excessive.', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Jul 09, 2013', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    balance: [
      { text: 'Not knowing exactly where that battery is placed, do you think it possible for lighter (smaller) batteries to also be used and still maintain CG?', author: 'vleisie', date: 'Mar 04, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Specify the center of gravity and position of the battery.', author: 'vleisie', date: 'Mar 04, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Quote: Originally Posted by vleisie The polaris uses down thrust because the motor is behind the cg.', author: 'orcas flier', date: 'Mar 23, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'This is standard for motors mounted high and close to the cg.', author: 'orcas flier', date: 'Mar 23, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Thanks Lockey The polaris uses down thrust because the motor is behind the cg.', author: 'vleisie', date: 'Mar 22, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'CG is spot on if not biased forward with the battery tucked up to the nose.', author: 'dz1sfb', date: 'Mar 14, 2013', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    finishing: [
      { text: 'Because of the increased size (52" span) and material mix, I have to really think ahead to avoid getting painted into a corner.', author: 'AlphaWhisky', date: 'May 13, 2013', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    flightNotes: [
      { text: 'I have not flown it from water, but taxi tests did not reveal any problems.', author: 'vleisie', date: 'Feb 25, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'It looked to be pretty wild in the air, maybe its tail heavy 2.', author: 'Wilfor', date: 'Jul 12, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'i added a pic to show what may help you get more thrust comparing it to the original design have you flown it off land or are you going straight for the water maiden ?', author: 'Wilfor', date: 'Jul 12, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'The wind calmed a bit this afternoon so I headed for the club field for a maiden.', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Mar 27, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Instead, I thought I would taxi/scoot around on the grass and get some feel for the ground handling.', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Mar 27, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Water taxi turning authority is good at very slow speed but not so good at moderate and higher speeds.', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Apr 15, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'All in all, I\'m happy with my Mermaid\'s performance off water and grass, and it\'s a pussycat in the air.', author: 'G550Ted', date: 'Apr 15, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I only flew with 70% low rate of recommended aileron and it is plenty unless you want to make very rapid rolls.', author: 'vleisie', date: 'Apr 01, 2013', source: 'thread' },
    ],
