    materials: [
      { text: 'Data Wing span: 72 cm (28.3 in) Length: 101 cm (39.7 in) The dimensions for the slots and notches are made for 6 mm depron.', author: 'tomhe', date: 'Oct 14, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I think that I have the same issue, since my Mig is mostly 3mm depron.', author: 'Shadegrown', date: 'Jul 22, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'The dimensions for the slots and notches are made for 6 mm depron.', author: 'segraves', date: 'Oct 18, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I\'ve decided to make a 1/2 scale version since I have a spare 3mm depron sheet and I want to try a pocket size fighter I\'m planning to use aileron/taileron linking.', author: 'Shadegrown', date: 'Oct 16, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'It took me some time, but I\'m finally building the Mig-29 in 1:2 scale from 3mm depron I\'m going to use a 2550kv 23g outrunner with apc 4.75x5.5 prop.', author: 'Shadegrown', date: 'Mar 25, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Quote: Originally Posted by Shadegrown I\'ve decided to make a 1/2 scale version since I have a spare 3mm depron sheet and I want to try a pocket size fighter I\'m planning to use aileron/taileron linking.', author: 'tomhe', date: 'Oct 16, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Quote: Originally Posted by Shadegrown It took me some time, but I\'m finally building the Mig-29 in 1:2 scale from 3mm depron Sounds very interesting.', author: 'tomhe', date: 'Mar 25, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'hi guis, my little Mig29 6mm depron with e-impeller and Thrust Vectoring with another servo...', author: 'fabionet31', date: 'Dec 26, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I think I might be able to fix that problem by using a piece of carbon rod to connect the rudders vs.', author: 'Cdr.Instigator', date: 'Jan 21, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'oh yah, i use 5min epoxy to glue my velco to the lipo for my heli, but i notice it doesn\'t want to stick to the battery.', author: 'uniquexme', date: 'Jan 02, 2008', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    electronics: [
      { text: 'This construction features an openable hatch for easy access to the battery and electronics, as seen in this picture of my F-22.', author: 'tomhe', date: 'Oct 14, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'This plane can be built with only tailerons, but I have drawn out markings for ailerons and rudders too.', author: 'tomhe', date: 'Oct 14, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'If using both ailerons and tailerons they can be coupled together for easy servo installation.', author: 'tomhe', date: 'Oct 14, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'UPDATE: This plane is now also available as a kit with a power combo (motor, ESC, and propeller) from Grayson Hobby.', author: 'tomhe', date: 'Oct 14, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Setup : - 1820kv BL Motor - 7x5 E-APC Prop - 40A HobbyWing ESC - Full 4-channel Aileron, Rudder and Elevator', author: 'zhnme523', date: 'Feb 10, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'so i would pay more caution on the battery and motor mounting.', author: 'uniquexme', date: 'Jan 02, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'My frenz F117, also faced the similar issue that day, his motor and motor mount ripped off, battery drop out, also cannot be found.', author: 'uniquexme', date: 'Jan 02, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I have finish building this MIG-29, but i check out the photo here that there are different ways to attach the servo.', author: 'uniquexme', date: 'Jan 02, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'May i ask if it flies better with both the aileron and elevator attached together to one servo on each side?', author: 'uniquexme', date: 'Jan 02, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'or shd i do it like the F18 way with aileron on the side and elevator on the rear?', author: 'uniquexme', date: 'Jan 02, 2008', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    balance: [
      { text: 'I was surprised that it was perfectly balanced from the initial first toss.', author: 'Cdr.Instigator', date: 'Jan 21, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Now I have the problem that I have a lot of weight on the right side, as I concentrated everything around the receiver to save on extension (I put the BEC on the left as the cables were long enough) I might end up using another extension…', author: 'Gosa77', date: 'Feb 13, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I used the CG position from earlier in the thread, scaled up and it was fine.', author: 'RobinBennett', date: 'Nov 04, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'On the test flight I had the cg way too far aft and crashed about 200 feet away and broke the nose off.', author: 'eliworm', date: 'Nov 09, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Center of Gravity I have set it at 2 and a 1/2 inches from the start of the leading edge of the wing..', author: 'Cdr.Instigator', date: 'Jan 16, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Mine is rather twitchy, and I\'m not sure if it\'s because I\'ve got massive control throws or the CG far enough back to fly inverted with no trim.', author: 'electriceye', date: 'Dec 06, 2007', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    finishing: [
      { text: 'Hi all, Some really nice planes on here, great paint jobs too!', author: 'colmoore', date: 'Mar 08, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'What does everyone use to paint their models with?', author: 'colmoore', date: 'Mar 08, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I\'m wondering what\'s best to go for, a spray on paint or an acrylic type poster paint.', author: 'colmoore', date: 'Mar 08, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I used some cheap spray cans so the result isn\'t very good.', author: 'tomhe', date: 'Oct 28, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Capt-Great paint scheme-Like you \'rainy day paint project, although I don\'t think mine will turn out as good as yours, very nice!!!', author: 'electriceye', date: 'Dec 08, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I\'m also done cutting up your F-22, just need to assemble and paint.', author: 'crxmanpat', date: 'Dec 19, 2007', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    flightNotes: [
      { text: 'The vid is evidence that you built it well and flew it well as well....thats a lot of wells!', author: 'Mordte', date: 'Mar 05, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Ha ha, at one point during the maiden a local dogwalkers mutt started humping my leg, ewww.', author: 'Mordte', date: 'Mar 05, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'A mixture of pure first flight fear and "get this goddam dog off me !!" type of thing.', author: 'Mordte', date: 'Mar 05, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I had the throws set real low as I haven\'t flown in over six years.', author: 'Wynterhawk', date: 'Nov 27, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'The Mig flew right out of my hand as I did the ol underhand toss at half throttle.', author: 'Wynterhawk', date: 'Nov 27, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'You see, ive never flown anything other than my Kyosho Citabria and the Air Hogs F-18.', author: 'Mordte', date: 'Mar 04, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I was confident but there was a nagging feeling of impending doom hanging over the maiden flight.', author: 'Mordte', date: 'Mar 04, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I took my Mig-29 for it\'s maiden flight during my lunch break to a field not far from here.', author: 'Cdr.Instigator', date: 'Jan 21, 2009', source: 'thread' },
    ],
