    problems: [
      {
        title: 'The main reason I put a fixed stab on this one is that it does help…',
        problem: 'The main reason I put a fixed stab on this one is that it does help the "digging in" issue at landing, and if this model is loaded down with heavy motors and batteries for speed it might land a little hot.',
        fix: 'Plus a fixed stab would be less inclined to flutter than a flying stab, which is good for a high-speed model.',
        author: 'jetset44', date: 'Oct 30, 2005',
      },
      {
        title: 'I solved the issue about elevators, by doing a sort of "Y" linkage to…',
        problem: 'I solved the issue about elevators, by doing a sort of "Y" linkage to 1 servo just in front of the motor depron piece.',
        fix: 'The thread does not record a fix for this.',
        author: 'testpilot', date: 'Mar 06, 2006',
      },
      {
        title: 'My only problem, is that in order to get the plane to balance, I had…',
        problem: 'My only problem, is that in order to get the plane to balance, I had to wedge my 1500 3s1P battery all the way up in the nose in a very tight fit.',
        fix: 'I also had to put my receiver literally about an inch away from the battery in order to get everything to balance.',
        author: 'TGK', date: 'Jun 11, 2006',
      },
    ],
