    electronics: [
      { text: 'Some technical questions: Since the elevator is split on the Voyager making elevons, how are these controlled with just one servo?', author: 'Gingy', date: 'Dec 16, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I\'ve never held a servo in my hands, but what I picture is two control horns.', author: 'Gingy', date: 'Dec 16, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'When the servo is activated in one direction it causes both horns in the servo arm to move, which would equate to one elevator up, and one down.', author: 'Gingy', date: 'Dec 16, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'How do both elevons operate together AND seperately using just one servo?', author: 'Gingy', date: 'Dec 16, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Do you wire the throttle out on the receiver to the ESC, which hen controls the speed of the motor?', author: 'Gingy', date: 'Dec 16, 2011', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'It was actually finished back in Feb, but needed an extension cable for elev servo.', author: 'ksqm', date: 'Oct 01, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Still have to decide if I\'ll go with an AP-05 3000kV or AP-03 4000kV motor.', author: 'ksqm', date: 'Oct 01, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Both are 2S capable, so I\'ll use an XP-7a ESC.', author: 'ksqm', date: 'Oct 01, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Have TP 250mAh 2S 20C or Hyperion 180mAh 2S 20C batts.', author: 'ksqm', date: 'Oct 01, 2013', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Initial test placement of electronics, indicates I can get everything placed behind the prop slot.', author: 'ksqm', date: 'Oct 01, 2013', source: 'thread' },
    ],
