    threads: [
      { url: 'http://www.rcgroups.com/forums/showthread.php?t=779331', label: 'RC GROUPS BUILD THREAD', external: true },
    ],
    materials: [
      { text: 'I\'m building mine from 6mm depron and 85% scale.', author: 'efether', date: 'Mar 01, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I will probably use foam longerons from the root to the tip on top of the bluecore then sheet it with 1mm depron.', author: 'UBILDIT', date: 'Dec 08, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'So...I finally got around to building my second one...this time out of Depron.', author: 'efether', date: 'Feb 23, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I used 6mm Depron for the main wing and fuse, and used 3mm depron over the top part of the wing to bury the CF and servos, as well as create a cambered wing.', author: 'efether', date: 'Feb 23, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Because i built the whole thing out of Elmer\'s Foamboard, which is extremely compact foam sandwiched between 2 sheets of construction paper, heavy, but strong, nothing broke except for the prop and a vertical stabilizer which i built out…', author: 'annihil8ted', date: 'Feb 12, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'The wing is actually a 6mm depron plate as per the original.', author: 'Kombatant', date: 'Feb 04, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Then pulled a top skin of 3mm depron over that.', author: 'Kombatant', date: 'Feb 04, 2009', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'With the foam, I use 15min epoxy for the wing spars, low-temp hot glue gun, 3M 77 spray for laminating, and sometimes foam-safe CA with kicker (accelerator).', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 14, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'For what it\'s worth, I build everything with 6mm Depron now.', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 14, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'i went to my hobby shop and he is out of the 6mm depron.', author: 'spadman82', date: 'Jan 07, 2009', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    electronics: [
      { text: 'First...here\'s my setup: Motor: SUPPO 2212-06 ESC: Suppo 30 Amp Prop: APC 5x5 Battery: TP 3S1320 Servos: Tower Pro 9g Receiver/Radio: AR6100E / Spektrum DX7 AUW: 13.1 oz.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I pulled up on the Elevator, and that plane snapped into a Cobra so fast...it was going...50-60 MPH, I pull back on the stick...and that thing snapped vertical and stopped!!!', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I rammed the throttle full and pushed down on the stick to get it back into normal flight...but it still hung there...I manually pushed the canard down.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'When the canard was active in the mix...the X-41 is HYPER SENSITIVE to any and all elevator movements.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I tested the plane where I used the canard for the elevator and left the Elevons neutral.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'It tracked in the vertical as any plane with a conventional elevator would.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I also tested it with reduced throttle, with full up canard and full down elevon...it slowed to a crawl, as the canard acted as a speed brake, yet flew level.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I would put the canard to the rudder channel, so it can be controlled independently of the elevons.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'If the canard is to be mixed with the elevator, set up the radio where you can turn the mix on or off.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'As a consideration for the less advanced pilot, put the canards on the elevator channel and use the main-wings controls as ailerons only.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    balance: [
      { text: 'That morning, I had even remeasured the entire plane and plugged-in all the numbers into a canard CG calculator I found in the canard thread just to plan for success as much as possible.', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 29, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'With the TP 3s1320, I would estimate the need to add about 1/4 oz of ballast to the nose.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Now that the CG is to my liking, I\'m feeling more like experimenting.', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Mar 10, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'That should fix it.....and probably force more balance weight in the nose.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 29, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'If you use a 2100 or 2200 mAh pack, it should be about right...I had to add 3/4 oz to the nose to get it to balance.', author: 'efether', date: 'Mar 01, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Also, the CG point on the plans seem to be too far to the rear...again, own personal experience.', author: 'efether', date: 'Mar 01, 2008', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    finishing: [
      { text: 'Wingspan: 28" AUW: 17oz Power: 2212-06 motor, 30A ESC, 3S 2100mAh 20C (about 230W with a 5.5x4.5 prop) Paint Scheme: Ukraine SU-27 in honor of my dearly departed Flanker (see my blog).', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 29, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Paint Used: Anita\'s All Purpose Acrylic Craft Paint from Hobby Lobby.', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 29, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Finished off with several coats of Minwax Semi-Gloss Polycrylic spray (blue can).', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 29, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I then used craft paint from hobby lobby (ceramcoat) for the darker blue, gray, and white.', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 13, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I then finished it all up with Minwax Polycrylic clear coat spray.', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 13, 2008', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'The decals were custom made from images I found on the intarweb.', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 13, 2008', source: 'thread' },
    ],
    flightNotes: [
      { text: 'The weather wouldn\'t cooperate for the maiden flight until Tuesday.', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 29, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Tuesday at lunch I drove to the field and met my friends there for my maiden.', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 29, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I throttled-up and it flew right out of my hand (in a good way).', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 29, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'I landed and adjusted, flew and landed and adjusted some more.', author: 'T3chDad', date: 'Nov 29, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'Decided to grab the ol\' X-41 and take it out for her maiden flight.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'On launch, I had the canard locked in place and I flew it as a Delta Wing.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'As a Delta flier (Canard locked), it flew very well.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
      { text: 'It might be my cambered wing mod that helped, but it flew very nice at all speed ranges, from slow to fast.', author: 'efether', date: 'Dec 23, 2007', source: 'thread' },
    ],
